stringJoinT -- the string join, `string $...$`, in an action body on both grammars (full monty plan step 1, stroke 1:
fixit newRoadStringJoin). The join builds a string from print items, as print does, and hands it back as a value:
$ ... $ joins with no spaces, plain items are spaced as print spaces them.

This file is not run alone. pop.sh builds two inputs per row, one process each under an alarm: everything above this
file's stop(), then on the OLD road (incant/grammar) a call of the row's action; on the NEW road (kantGrammar) sjNew on it
(which prints SJ BUILT <name> 1 when the body builds), then the call. A sentinel on stderr ends each. The old road is the
control: each row's value must be the same on both.

Before the stroke a body holding `string $...$` did not build on kantGrammar at all (the whole body was lost); tester's
show, showFinish and showForm were lost that way. SJ-7 builds those three and showStage on kantGrammar.
SJ-6 reaches the same join twice: an action must never change its own parse tree (bear-trap 22).

